{'data': {'actor_id': '01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771', 'created_at': '2026-09-21T20:32:31.940Z', 'event_type': 'comment.status_changed', 'id': '24', 'payload': {'from': 'open', 'reason': 'CONFIRMED and fixed in 10a2332b. Sharp catch — this defeated a guard by building on top of it.\n\nVerified: inARepository returned false for ANY error from resolveFactsTarget, and localRepoIdentityConflictError (env.go:152) is one of them. That error exists precisely to refuse to guess between two repository identity keys, and its message points at `repo-identity --keep`. Treating it as "not in a repository" swallowed it and filed a repo-scoped fact globally, silently.\n\nFix: inARepository now returns (bool, error) and classifies with errors.As — an ordinary not-a-repository error still falls back to global, an identity conflict is returned and surfaced by runRemember. The two cases call for opposite responses and are now distinguished rather than merged.\n\nProof: TestUndecidableRepositoryIdentityIsSurfacedNotFiledGlobally requires the conflict to be recognised through wrapping (the form it arrives in) and requires an ordinary not-a-repository error NOT to be mistaken for one. Removing the errors.As branch turns it red.', 'to': 'resolved'}, 'review_id': '01M32EBRXGJ7JNG04VAB5YAQ5B', 'target_id': '01M32EBRXVHTAR9GJBY7JVF5JE', 'target_type': 'review_comment', 'trail_id': '01M32E3Z5RX52805K6R7JZMCXS'}, 'event': 'comment.status_changed'}
{'data': {'actor_id': '01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771', 'created_at': '2026-09-21T20:32:33.455Z', 'event_type': 'comment.status_changed', 'id': '25', 'payload': {'from': 'open', 'reason': "CONFIRMED and fixed in 10a2332b.\n\nVerified: merged global facts flowed into factsLocusDrift(repoDir, matches) unchanged, one line above the semantic-cache exclusion that already handles them. Any global fact whose locus names a concrete file is absent from every repository except the one it was written in, so recall annotated it `stale locus` everywhere.\n\nOne refinement to the analysis: only locus tokens shaped like file paths are checked (locusTokenIsFilePath requires an extension), so a fact citing a bare directory was never flagged. The problem is real for the common case of a fact citing an actual file.\n\nFix: factsEligibleForLocusDrift drops global facts before the check.\n\nProof: TestLocusDriftSkipsGlobalFacts asserts the global fact is not flagged AND that the repository's own missing-locus fact still is — so the filter scopes the check rather than disabling it. Making the function return matches unchanged turns it red.\n\nTwo attempts were needed to get a test that could fail at all: the first reimplemented the filter inside the test, so it passed whatever the production code did, and the second used a bare directory as the locus, which the drift check never examines.", 'to': 'resolved'}, 'review_id': '01M32EBRXGJ7JNG04VAB5YAQ5B', 'target_id': '01M32EBRY3TC5WYW781BXGKAK4', 'target
