{'data': {'actor_id': '01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771', 'created_at': '2026-09-21T21:16:15.066Z', 'event_type': 'comment.status_changed', 'id': '42', 'payload': {'from': 'open', 'reason': 'CONFIRMED and fixed in 406465b1. The docs claim was the giveaway and it was right.\n\n`facts retract --global` shipped without its counterpart, so a global fact could be retracted and never pruned. The store grew without bound, and docs/reference.md\'s "the same retraction and garbage collection" was false.\n\nFix: `facts gc --global`, refusing --branch alongside it for the same reason retract does.\n\nScope note on the rest of the list: reclassify, promote and review are left repo-only deliberately. They operate on proposals and review queues that the global store does not have — there is no distill pipeline writing global facts, so there is nothing queued to promote or reclassify. gc was different because retraction already writes dead records there, and nothing could remove them. If a global distill path is ever added, those three come with it.\n\nProof: TestGlobalFactsCanBeGarbageCollected retracts a global fact and requires gc --global to remove it; removing the flag turns it red. TestGlobalGCRefusesABranch holds the flag conflict.', 'to': 'resolved'}, 'review_id': '01M32V15H59HTPNTN9ZZ8WJ7PJ', 'target_id': '01M32V15HGS6HDW324HN75DN21', 'target_type': 'review_comment', 'trail_id': '01M32E3Z5RX52805K6R7JZMCXS'}, 'event': 'comment.status_changed'}
